<% content_for :title, "Time Capsule | Bipolar Sober" %>

<main class="capsule-page">

  <style>
    .capsule-pet-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 24px;
    }

    .capsule-pet-card {
      min-width: 0;
      margin: 0;
    }

    .capsule-pet-image {
      display: block;
      width: 100%;
      height: auto;
      margin-bottom: 18px;
    }

    .capsule-pet-card h3 {
      margin: 0 0 12px;
    }

    .capsule-pet-card p {
      margin: 0 0 16px;
    }

    .capsule-pet-card p:last-child {
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }

    @media (max-width: 767px) {
      .capsule-pet-grid {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }
    }
  </style>


  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="capsule-hero">

    <picture class="capsule-background" aria-hidden="true">
      <source
        media="(min-width: 768px)"
        srcset="<%= asset_path('toolbox_time_capsule_desktop.webp') %>"
      >
      <%= image_tag "toolbox_time_capsule_mobile.webp",
          alt: "",
          loading: "eager" %>
    </picture>

    <div class="capsule-hero-content">

      <p class="capsule-eyebrow">
        BIPOLAR SOBER / TOOLBOX / TIME CAPSULE
      </p>

      <h1>
        <span>OPEN WHEN</span>
        <span>YOUR BRAIN</span>
        <span>FORGETS.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="capsule-intro">
        A NOTE FROM THE VERSION OF YOU<br>
        WHO REMEMBERS WHAT MATTERS.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 01 / A NOTE TO YOURSELF -->
  <section class="capsule-section capsule-pink">
    <div class="capsule-inner">

      <p class="capsule-number">01 / A NOTE TO YOURSELF</p>

      <h2>
        DEAR<br>
        FUTURE ME.
      </h2>

      <div class="capsule-copy">
        <p>
          Maybe you're feeling heavy, maybe your brain
          is moving faster than you can keep up with. Maybe you're somewhere
  in between, trying to figure out what the hell is happening. 
          Not sure what you're going through today or what kind of day 
          you're having.
        </p>

        <p>
          I’m writing this to remind you that one mood is not the whole
          story. You’ve had more than one kind of day, and you will have
          more. You don’t have to solve your entire life from inside this
          particular moment.
        </p>

        <p>
          Start with what’s actually in front of you. Take the next step
          you can manage. Let this note be a reminder that you’re still
          here, still figuring things out, and still allowed to begin
          again.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="capsule-callout">
        <p>
          YOU DON’T HAVE TO FEEL LIKE YOURSELF<br>
          TO DESERVE CARE FROM YOURSELF.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 02 / WHAT MATTERS -->
  <section class="capsule-section capsule-black">
    <div class="capsule-inner">

      <p class="capsule-number">02 / WHAT MATTERS</p>

      <h2>
        HERE'S WHAT<br>
        I WANT YOU TO<br>
        REMEMBER.
      </h2>

      <div class="capsule-copy">
        <p>
          
          You care about your family, your friends, your neighbors, and
          the connections you've worked to build. You care about Banjo and the things that
          make you laugh and the ordinary parts of life that can disappear
          from view when your mood takes over.
                  </p>

        <p>
        You care about sobriety because you want to be present for your life.
        You care about makign things with your hands, learning, reading,
        coding, being outside, and having room to discover what's next.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="capsule-grid">

        <div class="capsule-box">
          <h3>WHAT YOU CARE ABOUT.</h3>
          <p>
            Your relationships, your creativity, your sobriety, your health,
            and the life you're building one decision at a time.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="capsule-box">
          <h3>WHAT YOU WANT TO PROTECT.</h3>
          <p>
            Your recovery, your sense of self, your connections with people
            who care about you, and the choices you want to keep having.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="capsule-box">
          <h3>WHAT YOU'RE WORKING TOWARD.</h3>
          <p>
            More stability, more independence, more creative work,
            and a life that has room for both responsibility and fun.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="capsule-box">
          <h3>WHAT MAKES LIFE FEEL LIKE YOURS.</h3>
          <p>
            Making things, being curious, laughing at dumb shit,
            caring about people, and choosing what you want your days
            to be about.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 03 / PROOF -->
  <section class="capsule-section capsule-yellow">
    <div class="capsule-inner">

      <p class="capsule-number">03 / PROOF</p>

      <h2>
        YOU'VE BEEN<br>
        THROUGH SOME<br>
        SHIT.
      </h2>

      <div class="capsule-copy">
        <p>
          When your brain says you’ve made no progress, check the record.
          You’ve faced hard things, lived through consequences, and kept
          working on what comes next. That doesn’t make every day easy.
          It does mean this day isn’t the only evidence you have.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="capsule-grid">

        <div class="capsule-box">
          <h3>WHAT YOU'VE SURVIVED.</h3>
          <p>
            Jail. DUIs. Addiction. Learning to live with bipolar disorder.
            Long stretches when your mood made ordinary life feel far away.
            You're still here, and you're still building.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="capsule-box">
          <h3>WHAT YOU'RE PROUD OF.</h3>
          <p>
            The work you've done to understand yourself, the times you've asked
            for support, the things you've made, and every choice that helped
            me stay present for your life.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <div class="capsule-callout">
        <p>
          PROGRESS DOESN’T DISAPPEAR<br>
          JUST BECAUSE YOU CAN’T FEEL IT RIGHT NOW.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 04 / DIFFERENT DAYS -->
  <section class="capsule-section capsule-purple">
    <div class="capsule-inner">

      <p class="capsule-number">04 / DIFFERENT DAYS</p>

      <h2>
        HERE'S A<br>
        NOTE FOR YOU.
      </h2>

      <div class="capsule-copy">
        <p>
          Different moods can make different things feel true. These
          reminders aren’t orders.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="capsule-grid">

        <div class="capsule-box">
          <h3>WHEN EVERYTHING FEELS POINTLESS.</h3>
          <p>
            You don’t have to manufacture hope or fix the whole future.
            Make the day smaller. Do the next thing you can manage.
            This mood is real, but it isn’t the only version of your life.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="capsule-box">
          <h3>WHEN EVERYTHING FEELS POSSIBLE.</h3>
          <p>
            Enjoy the energy without letting urgency make every decision.
            You don’t have to act on every idea tonight. Give the plan time
            to exist tomorrow, too.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="capsule-box">
          <h3>WHEN I WANT TO ESCAPE.</h3>
          <p>
            Remember what alcohol promised and what it left behind.
            You can want relief without choosing the thing that has caused
            you harm. Let the urge pass through the moment before you
            decide what to do.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="capsule-box">
          <h3>WHEN YOU FORGET YOUR PROGRESS.</h3>
          <p>
            Look at what you’ve actually done, not just what remains
            unfinished. One hard day does not erase the work, the changes,
            or the choices you’ve made.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 05 / THE DAY I SAW THE UNIVERSE -->
  <section class="capsule-section capsule-black">
    <div class="capsule-inner">

      <p class="capsule-number">05 / THE DAY I SAW THE UNIVERSE</p>

      <h2>
        THE DAY<br>
        I SAW THE<br>
        UNIVERSE.
      </h2>

      <div class="capsule-copy">
        <p>
          By then, I was only a fraction of an iota spiritual. I believed
          in lucky license plates, but mostly as a game. If a plate started
          with the first three letters of Your old one—CQQ—I took it as a
          sign that the day might go well. Otherwise, I was completely
          jaded. The only miracles I believed in were Amazon packages
          arriving a day early.
        </p>

        <p>
          Then gabapentin—the medication I’d basically written off as a
          placebo—actually worked. At what I jokingly called a dog-level
          dosage, it eased the bilateral sciatica that had been making me
          hobble around rehab on a crutch. I threw the crutch aside in
          ecstasy.
        </p>

        <p>
          “Fuck this thing!”
        </p>

        <p>
          Then I walked back to pick it up. I stopped shuffling across
          the parking lot. I proudly carried Your own lunch tray. I carried
          whatever I could. I was so happy that, with Your spirituality
          just beginning to bud, I asked Bill if we could do a celebration
          ritual.
        </p>

        <p>
          Bill was an older fellow with long white hair and the biggest
          smile I’d ever seen.
        </p>

        <p>
          The day we met up, he said we needed to gather a couple of
          things. He took me to his car, and I stopped in Your tracks.
          His license plate read <strong>CQQ</strong>.
        </p>

        <p>
          I couldn’t believe it.
        </p>

        <p>
          From his car, I took an arrow. Then we went to an office where
          he retrieved a bow. We walked up the 12 Step Trail, stopping
          so I could rest Your legs. We talked the whole way. He gave me
          advice about sobriety, and I kept climbing.
        </p>

        <p>
          At the top, Bill handed me the arrow and told me to meditate
          on it—to think about Your sciatica. In private, I thought about
          all the ways pain had shaped Your life: the times it had led me
          to drink, Your first DUI, and the years it had hurt me.
        </p>

        <p>
          When I finished, he led me to a ledge. He showed me how to
          shoot, then told me where to aim.
        </p>

        <blockquote>
          “Those aspens are sacred, and this mountain is sacred.
          It will take your pain away.”
        </blockquote>

        <p>
          I nocked the arrow, aimed, and released it.
        </p>

        <p>
          As soon as I let it fly, I saw the Universe.
        </p>

        
      </div>

      <div class="capsule-grid">

        <div class="capsule-box">
  <h3>MEMORIES I WANT TO KEEP.</h3>

  <p>
    “You need to move out,” my roommate told me. The guy in the basement
    was complaining about me, the other roommates were complaining about
    my drinking, and everyone was complaining about Banjo.
    <em>Fine.</em>
  </p>

  <p>
    I was looking through Zillow when I saw an apartment available in the
    mountains. The rent was higher than I wanted, but I figured I’d go see
    it anyway. I drove up to Jamestown, parked in a dirt lot, and realized
    I had no idea how I was supposed to meet the landlord without cell
    service.
  </p>

  <p>
    I asked a group of old men drinking under a tree where 108 Main Street
    was. They pointed across the street to the Jamestown Mercantile, a
    restaurant. I awkwardly made conversation with them for a few minutes
    before a skinny older man appeared and introduced himself as the
    landlord. We went upstairs to see the apartment.
  </p>

  <p>
    The pictures didn’t do it justice. It was a gorgeous, three-level
    apartment. It was perfect. <em>This is mine</em>, I thought. I jumped
    on it immediately.
  </p>

  <p>
    “I have a place to go,” I proudly told my roommates. I started making
    plans, packing my things, and arranging to get the fuck out of Boulder.
    I’d lasted about eight months in that god-awful town, and I was happy
    to be leaving.
  </p>

  <p>
    On moving day, I listened to victory music all the way up the canyon.
    I was celebrating my escape from crime, streetlights, concrete, and my
    awful roommates. I was going to live in the mountains, in the forest,
    and among people in an actual community.
  </p>

  <p>
    That is how I found Jamestown.
  </p>
</div>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 06 / Your BEST FRIENDS -->
  <section class="capsule-section capsule-purple">
    <div class="capsule-inner">

      <p class="capsule-number">06 / Your BEST FRIENDS</p>

      <h2>
        THE ONES<br>
        WHO WERE<br>
        HOME.
      </h2>

      <div class="capsule-copy">
        <p>
          
        </p>

        <p>
          Banjo became your best friend, too. I want to remember how I met
          him and how much your life changed when he came home with me.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="capsule-pet-grid">

        <figure class="capsule-box capsule-pet-card">
          <%= image_tag "quil.jpg",
              alt: "Quil, Your guinea pig and best friend for a long time.",
              class: "capsule-pet-image",
              loading: "lazy" %>

          <figcaption>
            <h3>QUIL.</h3>
            <p>
              Quil was your guinea pig and your best friend for a long time.
          Remember how important Quil was to you, and that
          friendship doesn’t count for less just because Quil was small
          and furry and had a different kind of life. He was by your side for college,
          your move to Atlanta, and every heartbreak and everything in between.
            </p>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <figure class="capsule-box capsule-pet-card">
          <%= image_tag "banjo.jpg",
              alt: "Banjo, Your dog and best friend.",
              class: "capsule-pet-image",
              loading: "lazy" %>

          <figcaption>
            <h3>BANJO.</h3>
            <p>
              We went to the shelter just to look at dogs and maybe meet
              one we might adopt. Your roommate arrived late because of
              traffic. The workers ushered us into a meet-and-greet room,
              and we met a few dogs. They were all cute, but when they
              brought in “Coffee,” I took one look at him and thought,
              <em>He’s mine.</em>
            </p>

            <p>
              That’s how I met Banjo. We took him home, and at first he
              was a little tornado. With training, he became a good boy.
              He’s been Your best friend for nine years.
            </p>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 07 / KEEP ADDING -->
  <section class="capsule-section capsule-pink">
    <div class="capsule-inner">

      <p class="capsule-number">07 / KEEP ADDING</p>

      <h2>
        YOU'RE STILL<br>
        WRITING<br>
        THIS THING.
      </h2>

      <div class="capsule-copy">
        <p>
          This note is one snapshot, not a set of rules for who I have to
          be. I can add to it as I learn more about what helps, what matters,
          and what I want Your life to hold.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="capsule-callout">
        <p>
          WHAT DO I WANT FUTURE ME TO REMEMBER<br>
          ABOUT THIS PART OF YOUR LIFE?
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- BACK TO TOOLBOX -->
  <nav class="index-home-nav" aria-label="Return to toolbox">
    <%= link_to "← BACK TO TOOLBOX",
        toolbox_path,
        class: "index-home-button" %>
  </nav>

</main>